slides.raw_text:
Casting in an Augmented Expression 
In Java, an augmented expression of the form
x1 op = x2
is implemented as x1 = (T)(x1 op x2), where T is the 
type for x1. Therefore, the following code is correct:
int sum = 0;
sum += 4.5; // sum becomes 4 after this statement
// This is equivalent to sum = (int)(sum + 4.5);

